* Out-of-range BSIM3 parameter. PCLM=0 is the natural way to write "no
* channel-length modulation", and it is what the long-channel reduction cards
* would say if the model allowed it. BSIM3's parameter check refuses the value:
*
*     Fatal: Pclm = 0 is not positive.
*     Fatal error: Fatal error(s) detected during BSIM3V3.3 parameter checking
*
* This is the one rejection in the channel that produces a DIAGNOSIS rather than
* a tokenizer error, and the reason the long-channel cards carry pclm=1e-12.
* It must be refused; a card that loaded here would silently mean a different
* model than it declares.
.model n1 nmos level=8 vth0=0.5 u0=600 tox=9n
+ pclm=0
